  "question": {
    ":question/id": "9e42324e-b194-5960-ac19-d09b25aae359",
    ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
    ":question/problem": "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\nx=t(t-2)-1,\\,y=t(1-t)-2,\\,-2\\le t\\le 2\n$$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=t(t-2)-1.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $7$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $-2$ | $-1$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=t(1-t)-2.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $7$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $-2$ | $-1$ |\n| $y$ | $-8$ | $-4$ | $-2$ | $-2$ | $-4$ |\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](images/67/671f539b58c5eeed927f86b97a2893f44a7bc9e6c0f776315e3f8c92090c4a0e.png)",
